winemac: programs go by their own name, tray icons show in the menu bar, window commands in the application menu

Every Wine program is the same Mac executable, so macOS called them all "wine" (or by the
loader bundle's name) in the menu bar, the Dock, the app switcher and Activity Monitor. A
program now gets the name FineWine lists it under (FINEWINE_APP_NAME, for the executable named
by FINEWINE_APP_EXE), else the product name or description from its version information, else
its file name. The name is stored before the Cocoa side starts and must not be handed to the
main thread from there: that creates the application controller too early, and menus hang.

Notification-area icons were given a custom view to draw in, which macOS no longer shows, so
they were invisible. They now use the status item's button. FINEWINE_TRAY_LOG=1 reports what
macOS made of an item.

The application menu gains what Windows offers on a taskbar button: Restore, Minimize,
Maximize and Close Window, for the front window. The Window menu is the Windows menu again
(it had become the View menu). The window side of the commands is in the next patch.

